    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0857" n="1815" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1815"/>

                <head>No. 58.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rives to Mr. Garland</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 17,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your letter of the 11th
                    instant, in relation to the postponement of the sale of the British schooners
                    condemned for taking seals in Behring Sea in 1887, I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith a copy of a note received yesterday from the British minister, bearing
                        <pb facs="0858" n="1816" xml:id="pg1816"/> date the 12th instant, on the
                    same subject; and shall be glad to receive an expression of your views on the
                    arrangement proposed by the British Government in regard to the disposition of
                    the vessels.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. L. Rives.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
